@jschmied the grouped commit is up as #61017, stacked on this PR (only the last commit is new). On XPU, for 3 KV cache groups × 6 GDN layers, it cut the commit's host time from about 400 to 140 µs per step. With PP=2 it lowered the single-stream decode slope by 0.19 ms/token. Your GB10 numbers (PP=1) would show how much it helps on CUDA.

Written with AI assistance (Claude Code).

— TSUMUGI-XE
